From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:21:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mesh LOD depth from the fade plane (viewport.r[1]), not the
 camera orientation quaternion; ed_lod_info camera diagnostics

MeshRenderer::Batch dotted each instance position with the first 16 bytes of the camera (the orientation quaternion) instead of its fadePlane argument (the camera's viewport.r[1], what the binary reads at 0x007DFB7F). The LOD depth therefore depended on the heading and flipped sign when the heading was reached by turning the other way round: units/props switched LOD and vanished when the camera only turned. New ed_lod_info([entityId]) returns eye position, heading, pitch, zoom, fov, the LOD plane, viewport and the selected LOD with its cutoffs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

